This paper investigates the existence of normalized ground state solutions to the biharmonic Choquard equation under exponential critical growth, with the prescribed functional being defined as
  \begin{align*}
  I(f)=\int_{\mathbb{R}^4}\left(|\Delta^2f|^2+|x|^{-\alpha}*|f|^2\right)\,dx.
  \end{align*}
  We assume that the values of $p$ and $\alpha$ satisfy the conditions $3< p<5$, and $\alpha$ can be any real number greater than $3-p$. The study utilizes variational methods and a combination of the concentration compactness principle and the monotone method of the minimization of action to demonstrate the presence of a natural transformation and a palais-smale sequence for the prescribed functional. As a result, we have shown the existence of a natural transformation and a palais-smale sequence for the prescribed functional.

